Z||000005||lowCG||08-06-2001||08:34 PM||||I'm adapting some 4 piston BMW calipers to fit my car with some machine work(offset bushings on both my hubs and on the calipers)to get them to fit.This has to be this way with these calipers because the bolt pattern is close to the Fiero pattern,but not the same.The calipers will mount directly to the outboard side of the Fiero mounting ears,after trueing the surface up a little to make for a super-flat mounting surface.<BR>I almost wish I had some 17" wheels so that I could just make an adapter bracket instead of the wierd little bushings/welding that I'm doing now.Too much $ for new wheels/tires though,besides,I'm committed to the plan I already have going,also,I haven't priced the Subaru SVX 12.9" rotors,and they may be expensive;the Outback 10.7" ones I have are pretty reasonable($35).<BR>||||reg||1
